            "relevance_3LNXgq": "- **Relevance Score:** 65/100\n- **Relevance Tag:** Somewhat Relevant\n- **Reasoning:** Uses correctional mental\u2011health data to detail prevalence and services for inmates; cites constitutional duty to provide care, linking to prisoner rights; does not address education levels or entry age.",
            "abstract_5B4jjq": "The prevalence of depression, psychosis, substance use, and attempted or completed suicide in incarcerated populations is higher than in the general community. Mental health services are important components of care provided to inmates and involve screening for potential mental illness, further assessment of identified mental illness, and the provision of care appropriate to the inmate\u2019s need. In the United States, there is a constitutional requirement to provide a level of care that demonstrates that correctional officials are not deliberately indifferent to the serious medical and mental health needs of those they incarcerate.",
            "education-lev_LZfD4h": "Not available in metadata.",
            "mental-health_Bk3U8f": "The prevalence of depression, psychosis, substance use, and attempted or completed suicide is higher in incarcerated populations than in the general community. Mental health services in prisons involve screening, assessment, and care provision appropriate to the inmate\u2019s needs. In the U.S., there is a constitutional requirement to provide care demonstrating that correctional officials are not deliberately indifferent to serious medical and mental health needs. Specific statistics on prevalence, service quality, barriers, medication access, crisis intervention, staff training, prisoner perceptions, or unmet needs are not detailed beyond the general statement of higher prevalence and constitutional requirement for care.",
            "prisoner-righ_Ulqd1Y": "In the United States, there is a constitutional requirement to provide a level of care that demonstrates correctional officials are not deliberately indifferent to the serious medical and mental health needs of those they incarcerate. Mental health services for inmates involve screening, assessment, and care provision appropriate to their needs. The paper highlights the higher prevalence of depression, psychosis, substance use, and suicide in incarcerated populations compared to the general community.",
            "prisoner-righ_UGCvQi": "In the United States, there is a constitutional requirement to provide a level of care, demonstrating that correctional officials are not deliberately indifferent to the serious medical and mental health needs of those they incarcerate. This establishes a legal right to care for incarcerated individuals. The paper highlights the importance of mental health services, including screening, assessment, and provision of appropriate care for inmates.",
            "mental-health_MAwBu4": "Incarcerated populations in the United States exhibit higher prevalence of depression, psychosis, substance use, and attempted or completed suicide compared to the general community. Mental health services include screening, assessment, and care provision. There is a constitutional requirement to provide a level of care demonstrating correctional officials are not deliberately indifferent to serious medical and mental health needs."
