                "tldr": "In this article, the authors present findings from a study conducted to examine the relationships between jails which were represented at the 1978 Special National Workshop on Mental Health Services in Local Jails and various components of their local mental health systems.",
                "podcast": null,
                "podcast_generation_allowed": true,
                "entity_type": "PAPER",
                "score": 0.5383771,
                "section_names": [
                    "Summary",
                    "PRINCIPLES FOR PLANNING JAIL MENTAL HEALTH PROGRAMS"
                ],
                "rank": 16,
                "relevance_data": {},
                "source": "scispace_full_text",
                "relevance_summary": "Uses jail mental health program data to illustrate service gaps; examines court orders and inmate lawsuits, highlighting rights and advocacy; no focus on education or entry age.",
                "relevance_metadata": {
                    "criteria_judgments": [
                        {
