                "tldr": "A whole prison approach to health and mental health will offer the greatest likelihood that offenders will thrive, benefit from imprisonment, and lead law-abiding lives after release, as well as creating a healthier and safer society.",
                "podcast": null,
                "podcast_generation_allowed": true,
                "entity_type": "PAPER",
                "rank": 14,
                "relevance_data": {},
                "source": "scispace",
                "relevance_summary": "Uses prison mental\u2011health agenda to argue for public\u2011health\u2011led services; directly addresses prisoners' mental health, mentions rights and public awareness, but does not examine education levels or entry age.",
                "relevance_metadata": {
                    "criteria_judgments": [
                        {
                            "criterion_name": "Incarcerated Population Focus",
                            "relevance": "Perfectly Relevant"
                        },
                        {
                            "criterion_name": "Educational Attainment of Prisoners",
                            "relevance": "Not Relevant"
                        },
                        {
                            "criterion_name": "Age at Incarceration Entry and Pathways",
                            "relevance": "Not Relevant"
                        },
                        {
                            "criterion_name": "Prisoner Rights, Voice, and Advocacy",
                            "relevance": "Somewhat Relevant"
                        },
                        {
                            "criterion_name": "Mental Health and Psychological Well\u2011Being of Prisoners",
                            "relevance": "Perfectly Relevant"
                        }
                    ]
                }
            },
            "relevance_3LNXgq": "- **Relevance Score:** 60/100\n- **Relevance Tag:** Somewhat Relevant\n- **Reasoning:** Uses prison mental\u2011health agenda to argue for public\u2011health\u2011led services; directly addresses prisoners' mental health, mentions rights and public awareness, but does not examine education levels or entry age.",
            "abstract_5B4jjq": "Mental illness affects the majority of prisoners. Mental health issues are beginning to take a central position in the development of prison health services, reflecting this burden of disease. This change in focus is not before time. But prison mental health services cannot exist in isolation. Public health systems should lead provision of care for patients with acute and severe illness. A whole prison approach to health and, specifically, mental health will offer the greatest likelihood that offenders will thrive, benefit from imprisonment, and lead law\u2010abiding lives after release. Public awareness of the scale and commitment of prisons to mental health and illness, and understanding of prisons\u2019 role in society, are necessary developments that would protect and enhance public mental health, as well as creating a healthier and safer society. This article draws on recent reviews, information and statements to set out a public health agenda for mental health in prisons.",
            "education-lev_LZfD4h": "",
            "mental-health_Bk3U8f": "",
            "prisoner-righ_Ulqd1Y": "",
            "prisoner-righ_UGCvQi": "",
            "mental-health_MAwBu4": ""
        },
        {
            "papers_Knp69H": {
                "id": 2064333723,
                "title": "Improving Psychiatric Care for Prisoners",
                "is_archived": false,
                "full_slug": "improving-psychiatric-care-for-prisoners-6pwtcqxwx8",
                "journal": {
                    "display_name": "Psychiatric Services",
                    "official_page": "http://psychservices.psychiatryonline.org/",
                    "issn": "1075-2730",
                    "alias": null,
                    "id": 171176648,
                    "slug": "psychiatric-services",
                    "unique_id": "3d2bwj69",
                    "full_slug": "psychiatric-services-3d2bwj69"
