        {
            "papers_Knp69H": {
                "id": 4042799145,
                "title": "Mental health",
                "is_archived": false,
                "full_slug": "mental-health-zkmn6ctq3s",
                "journal": null,
                "conference_series": null,
                "date": "2023-12-01 00:00:00+00:00",
                "is_oa": null,
                "publication_type": "Book Chapter",
                "doi": "10.1093/med/9780198834533.003.0008",
                "unique_id": "zkmn6ctq3s",
                "abstract": "Abstract Mental health issues are much more common in people residing in prison than the general population: depression, psychosis, and substance misuse have the strongest evidence of increased prevalence compared to the un-incarcerated population. The prison mental health service and levels of care are discussed, and the chapter moves on to mental health assessment, screening, emergency situations, and ways of conducting the assessment. Practical considerations, compulsory treatment, and transfer to hospital are all covered. Depression, psychosis and schizophrenia, personality disorders, attention deficit hyperactivity disorder, and post-traumatic stress disorder are all discussed. The management of people in prison with a history of sexual convictions, including release support, is explained. The principles of safer custody are included. The definitions and rationale for segregation and the duties of the healthcare workers and prison general practitioner are discussed, and the chapter concludes with the assessment of mental health risk and advocation for the vulnerable. ",
                "is_fulltext_request_allowed": false,
                "metrics": {
                    "citations": {
                        "total": null
                    }
                },
                "tldr": "Mental health issues are highly prevalent in prisoners, with depression, psychosis, and substance misuse being the most common. The chapter covers various aspects of mental health management within the prison system, including assessment, screening, treatment, and risk management.",
                "podcast": null,
                "podcast_generation_allowed": true,
                "entity_type": "PAPER",
                "rank": 24,
                "relevance_data": {},
