                "tldr": "It is a prudent activity for counselors to identify treatment programs that develop attitudes and skills that may promote optimal functioning in offenders following their release from incarceration, and the notable absence of group-based counseling interventions as a standard of care is concerning.",
                "podcast": null,
                "podcast_generation_allowed": true,
                "entity_type": "PAPER",
                "rank": 19,
                "relevance_data": {},
                "source": "scispace",
                "relevance_summary": "Uses ARRAY program to evaluate mental\u2011health group counseling for incarcerated offenders with mental illness; directly addresses prison mental\u2011health needs but does not cover education, entry age, rights advocacy, or cross\u2011jurisdiction comparisons.",
                "relevance_metadata": {
                    "criteria_judgments": [
                        {
                            "criterion_name": "Incarcerated Population Focus",
