            "relevance_3LNXgq": "- **Relevance Score:** 53/100\n- **Relevance Tag:** Somewhat Relevant\n- **Reasoning:** Uses prison inmate data to examine treatment impact; provides age-at-first\u2011incarceration stats; lacks education or rights focus; mentions therapeutic interventions suggesting mental\u2011health relevance and hints at inmate needs assessment.",
            "abstract_5B4jjq": "espanolSe ha realizado esta tesis doctoral con los siguientes objetivos: 1. Analizar las caracteristicas mas relevantes de una muestra de sujetos con problemas de drogas y que fueron excarcelados para cumplir una pena alternativa a la pena privativa de libertad en un centro terapeutico. 2. Estudiar las variables que tienen un mayor grado de asociacion con la reincidencia empirica penitenciaria. 3. Establecer la tasa de reincidencia 4. Revisar y reelaborar \ufffdel discurso de que nada funciona\ufffd en relacion con los programas de rehabilitacion de reclusos drogodependientes. Los resultados mas relevantes de este estudio para la prevencion de la reincidencia, nos llevan a concluir que: no tener habitos laborales, ser expulsado o abandonar el tratamiento y permanecer en tratamiento menos de seis meses son algunos de los factores dinamicos que se relacionan con la reincidencia. EnglishWas conducted this Doctoral Dissertation with the following objectives: 1. Analyzing the major characteristics of a sample of subjects with drug problems and who were released to comply an alternative to imprisonment in a therapeutic center. 2. Studying the variables that have a higher degree of association with the empirical prison recidivism. 3. Establish the rate of recidivism 4. Reviewing and re-elaborating \"the speech that nothing works\" in relation to rehabilitation programs for drug dependent prisoners. The most relevant results of this study for the crime prevention lead us to conclude that having no work habits, being expelled or leaving the treatment and remaining in treatment less than six months are some of the dynamic factors that relate to recidivism.",
            "education-lev_LZfD4h": "",
