                "link": "https://link.springer.com/article/10.1186/s12889-016-3555-2",
                "source": "scispace",
                "google_scholar_id": "-0F_QFL1mpIJ",
                "snippet": "\u2026 Collectively, this research highlights the differential selection among racial and ethnic minorities into the prison system which may influence the education-health association. \u2026",
                "rank": 5,
                "relevance_data": {},
                "relevance_summary": "Uses prison\u2011level fixed effects to link inmates' education (including GED attainment) with morbidity outcomes; focuses on incarcerated adults, but does not address entry age, rights, or advocacy, and only broadly touches mental health via general health conditions.",
                "relevance_metadata": {
                    "criteria_judgments": [
                        {
                            "criterion_name": "Incarcerated Population Focus",
                            "relevance": "Perfectly Relevant"
                        },
                        {
                            "criterion_name": "Educational Attainment of Prisoners",
                            "relevance": "Perfectly Relevant"
                        },
                        {
