        {
            "papers_Knp69H": {
                "id": 4014812574,
                "title": "The Human Rights of \u201cPrisoners\u201d",
                "is_archived": false,
                "full_slug": "the-human-rights-of-prisoners-i9qor7bx",
                "journal": null,
                "conference_series": null,
                "date": "2022-09-14 00:00:00+00:00",
                "is_oa": false,
                "publication_type": "Book Chapter",
                "doi": "10.4324/9781003111269-15",
                "unique_id": "i9qor7bx",
                "abstract": "This chapter provides an overview of the United Nations human rights and their classification of \u2018prisoners\u2019 as a vulnerable population with special needs groups. We move beyond the label of prisoners, accentuating that the focus is on people, not prisons. Therefore, throughout the chapter, we refer to this vulnerable population as people, not \u2018prisoners.\u2019 We paint their global portrait, reflecting on who they are and the issues that influence their pathways to prison and their access to justice. Drawing from the United Nations\u2019 theoretical and empirical knowledge basis, we take readers through a guided discovery to understand the conditions of the criminal justice system, especially the conditions of confinement and its influence on vulnerable individuals, families, and communities worldwide. We highlight the intersection of human rights in the role of social work in addressing the rights and needs of people in prison from diverse backgrounds and other intersectional identities. ",
                "is_fulltext_request_allowed": false,
                "metrics": {
                    "citations": {
                        "total": null
                    }
                },
                "tldr": "In this paper , an overview of the United Nations human rights and their classification of prisoners as a vulnerable population with special needs groups is provided. But the focus is on people, not prisons.",
