                "tldr": "There is a compelling logic to provide expansive education and training programs for adults under correctional supervision as mentioned in this paper, and these programs can prepare an underused pool of workers at a time when the nation is facing significant labor shortages.",
                "podcast": null,
                "podcast_generation_allowed": true,
                "entity_type": "PAPER",
                "score": 0.7295395,
                "section_names": [
                    "Literacy Needs of Offenders"
                ],
                "rank": 24,
                "relevance_data": {},
                "source": "scispace_full_text",
                "relevance_summary": "Uses NALS literacy data to detail inmates' education gaps and need for basic adult classes; focuses on prison population, not age entry, rights, or mental health.",
                "relevance_metadata": {
                    "criteria_judgments": [
                        {
                            "criterion_name": "Incarcerated Population Focus",
                            "relevance": "Perfectly Relevant"
