                    }
                },
                "tldr": "According to the US Department of Education (Linton, 2004), approximately 75 per cent of men and women released from prison will commit an additional crime within three years as mentioned in this paper, and the lack of financial resources for correctional education, coupled by the negative stigma associated with being an ex-convict contributes greatly to recidivism.",
                "podcast": null,
