                "tldr": "A literature review of the academic characteristics of incarcerated youth and the academic correctional education programs serving them was conducted as mentioned in this paper, which indicated incarcerated adolescents function in the low-average to below-average range of intelligence, perform academically between fifth-and ninth-grade levels, and have histories of high rates of academic failure and grade retention.",
                "podcast": null,
                "podcast_generation_allowed": true,
