        {
            "papers_Knp69H": {
                "id": 3095735471,
                "title": "Local Lads: Pathways to Prison",
                "is_archived": false,
                "full_slug": "local-lads-pathways-to-prison-3c6vpw93k4",
                "journal": null,
                "conference_series": null,
                "date": "2021-01-01 00:00:00+00:00",
                "is_oa": false,
                "publication_type": "Book Chapter",
                "doi": "10.1007/978-3-030-61059-3_5",
                "unique_id": "3c6vpw93k4",
                "abstract": "In Chapter 5, Maguire examines the participants\u2019 backgrounds to reveal which types of men constitute the bulk of the prison population in England and Wales. He explains how their journeys to \u201crevolving-door imprisonment\u201d started long before they first reached the courtrooms and prison gates. Analysing the sites in which they \u201clearned to become men\u201d, Maguire charts how their early experiences\u2014at home, in deprived neighbourhoods, in \u201ccare\u201d, at failing schools and of (un)employment\u2014led to pathways to imprisonment. Negotiating their identities across these spaces, the respondents\u2014from a young age\u2014invested heavily in what critical men\u2019s studies scholars term \u201cprotest\u201d masculinities. Maguire concludes by asserting that \u201cdoing masculinity\u201d across impoverished spaces incrementally leads to exclusion; every shift culminates in costly\u2014more marginalised\u2014masculine performances.",
                "authors": {
                    "total": 1,
                    "data": [
                        {
                            "display_name": "David Maguire",
                            "id": 3096075826,
                            "slug": "david-maguire",
                            "unique_id": "4xun3ja9ko",
