                        "total": null
                    }
                },
                "tldr": "In the UK, imprisonment formally constitutes the law's most severe penalty, and individuals who breach the fundamental tenets of the criminal law are removed from the rest of society, deprived of their freedom of movement, and subjected to numerous further constraints frequently amounting to an alteration in their legally recognized rights and liberties as mentioned in this paper.",
